{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019baxoiyPXXpBFEoSq98ECR","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\n     2→title: \"Build, lint, and version-check via mage targets\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs mage build to compile cmd/version to bin/version, verifies that the\n     6→  binary prints the repository's version tag, runs mage lint to confirm no warnings, and\n     7→  runs mage clean to remove build artifacts. This exercises the full build lifecycle\n     8→  specified in prd011-magefiles before any utility code exists.\n     9→\n    10→actor: Human Operator\n    11→\n    12→trigger: |\n    13→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd011-magefiles.yaml) and wants to verify that the\n    14→  build pipeline produces a working binary.\n    15→\n    16→flow:\n    17→  - id: F1\n    18→    step: |\n    19→      The operator runs mage build. The target compiles every package under cmd/ to bin/.\n    20→      For cmd/version, the target resolves the latest version tag via\n    21→      git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passes it through -ldflags.\n    22→  - id: F2\n    23→    step: |\n    24→      The operator runs bin/version. The binary prints the version tag (e.g., \"v0.20260228.0\")\n    25→      to stdout followed by a newline and exits 0.\n    26→  - id: F3\n    27→    step: |\n    28→      The operator runs bin/version --version. The output is identical to F2.\n    29→  - id: F4\n    30→    step: |\n    31→      The operator runs bin/version --bogus. The binary prints a usage message to stderr\n    32→      and exits 2.\n    33→  - id: F5\n    34→    step: |\n    35→      The operator runs mage lint. golangci-lint runs on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/ with\n    36→      no warnings or errors.\n    37→  - id: F6\n    38→    step: |\n    39→      The operator runs mage clean. The bin/ directory and its contents are removed. If\n    40→      bin/ does not exist, the target succeeds silently.\n    41→  - id: F7\n    42→    step: |\n    43→      The operator verifies that bin/ no longer exists after mage clean.\n    44→\n    45→touchpoints:\n    46→  - T1: \"cmd/version — version string printing, ldflags injection (prd011-magefiles R1)\"\n    47→  - T2: \"magefiles/ — build, lint, clean targets (prd011-magefiles R2, R3, R4)\"\n    48→  - T3: \"configuration.yaml — project.binary_dir, project.go_source_dirs (prd011-magefiles R6)\"\n    49→\n    50→success_criteria:\n    51→  - id: S1\n    52→    criterion: mage build succeeds and bin/version exists.\n    53→  - id: S2\n    54→    criterion: bin/version prints a version tag matching v[0-9]* and exits 0.\n    55→  - id: S3\n    56→    criterion: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n    57→  - id: S4\n    58→    criterion: bin/version --bogus prints to stderr and exits 2.\n    59→  - id: S5\n    60→    criterion: mage lint passes with no warnings on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/.\n    61→  - id: S6\n    62→    criterion: mage clean removes bin/ and succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n    63→  - id: S7\n    64→    criterion: A development build (no ldflags) produces a binary that prints \"dev\".\n    65→\n    66→out_of_scope:\n    67→  - Differential testing of cmd/version against a reference binary (there is no GNU version equivalent).\n    68→  - mage install is exercised by the operator manually; it is not part of this use case's primary flow.\n    69→  - Orchestrator, generator, scaffold, and prompt targets are provided by cobbler-scaffold and not covered here.\n    70→\n    71→test_suite: test-rel00.0\n    72→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60c70176-0c98-4706-bfda-3d71f24296c2","uuid":"55e88661-355c-4474-a239-64e9c7ed8222","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/93/docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc001-magefiles.yaml","content":"id: rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\ntitle: \"Build, lint, and version-check via mage targets\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs mage build to compile cmd/version to bin/version, verifies that the\n  binary prints the repository's version tag, runs mage lint to confirm no warnings, and\n  runs mage clean to remove build artifacts. This exercises the full build lifecycle\n  specified in prd011-magefiles before any utility code exists.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd011-magefiles.yaml) and wants to verify that the\n  build pipeline produces a working binary.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs mage build. The target compiles every package under cmd/ to bin/.\n      For cmd/version, the target resolves the latest version tag via\n      git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passes it through -ldflags.\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      The operator runs bin/version. The binary prints the version tag (e.g., \"v0.20260228.0\")\n      to stdout followed by a newline and exits 0.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      The operator runs bin/version --version. The output is identical to F2.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The operator runs bin/version --bogus. The binary prints a usage message to stderr\n      and exits 2.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The operator runs mage lint. golangci-lint runs on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/ with\n      no warnings or errors.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The operator runs mage clean. The bin/ directory and its contents are removed. If\n      bin/ does not exist, the target succeeds silently.\n  - id: F7\n    step: |\n      The operator verifies that bin/ no longer exists after mage clean.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/version — version string printing, ldflags injection (prd011-magefiles R1)\"\n  - T2: \"magefiles/ — build, lint, clean targets (prd011-magefiles R2, R3, R4)\"\n  - T3: \"configuration.yaml — project.binary_dir, project.go_source_dirs (prd011-magefiles R6)\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: mage build succeeds and bin/version exists.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: bin/version prints a version tag matching v[0-9]* and exits 0.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: bin/version --bogus prints to stderr and exits 2.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: mage lint passes with no warnings on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: mage clean removes bin/ and succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: A development build (no ldflags) produces a binary that prints \"dev\".\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Differential testing of cmd/version against a reference binary (there is no GNU version equivalent).\n  - mage install is exercised by the operator manually; it is not part of this use case's primary flow.\n  - Orchestrator, generator, scaffold, and prompt targets are provided by cobbler-scaffold and not covered here.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel00.0\n","numLines":72,"startLine":1,"totalLines":72}}}
